Falsifies `system_tests::user::raw_mode_tests::a_badged_copy_of_the_terminal_reads_keystrokes_and_cannot_type_them`.

Architecture: all three (the change is in a userspace component, `components/src/line_editor.rs`,
built for every ISA from one source; the table it reads is `crates/line_editor/src/proto.rs`'s
`admits`).

The defect this restores is the one milestone 709 closes: the boot line discipline served every
request the same whatever the badge on the capability that sent it, so a `graphical_terminal`
session holding a copy of its endpoint could `OPERATION_BYTES` a command line into the queue the boot shell
reads with `OPERATION_READLINE`. The patch lets the raw-only badge through the terminal's
allowlist whole (`RAW_ONLY_BADGE => true` in `proto::admits`), which is that guard removed for this badge.

Expected to fail: `assert_eq!(r[0], BAD_REQUEST, "a badged holder's OPERATION_BYTES was served (r0 = 0):
it can type a line the boot shell reads")`, the first assertion in the test. Under the patch the
discipline answers `0` and queues `ls`.

Replayed on 2026-10-03 (UTC) by the lane for milestone 709 (a graphical terminal session on the
no-keyboard arm holds only the raw half of the boot discipline); see the roadmap block for the exit
code and the assertion line. The first red was taken before the fix existed, which is the same
tree as this patch applied.

**Re-cut 2026-10-12 (UTC) by the long-function paydown lane**, when `_start`'s opcode match moved
into `Terminal::serve` and the guard came to sit ahead of that call instead. Same defect, same
lines removed. Replayed red on aarch64 the same day, at the same first assertion
(`raw_mode_tests.rs:449`).

**Re-cut 2026-10-24 (UTC) by maintainer/terminal-quiesce-from-supervisor-only**, when the serve
loop's allowlist moved into `line_editor::proto::admits` so `line_editor` and its host tests read
one table. Same defect, `RAW_ONLY_BADGE => true` there. Replayed red on aarch64 the same day, at
the same first assertion (`raw_mode_tests.rs:449`).

